---
/*
 * DataverseFitSelector.astro
 *
 * Purpose:
 * Helps readers decide whether a workload is a strong,
 * possible, or weak fit for Microsoft Dataverse.
 *
 * The selector follows the article's beginner mental model:
 * structured business data → relationships → security →
 * governance → Power Platform integration.
 *
 * Self-contained Astro component.
 */
---

<section
  class="dvfs"
  data-dvfs
  aria-labelledby="dvfs-title"
>
  <div class="dvfs__header">
    <div class="dvfs__header-copy">
      <p class="dvfs__eyebrow">Workload selector</p>

      <h3 id="dvfs-title">
        Is Dataverse a good fit for this workload?
      </h3>

      <p class="dvfs__intro">
        Choose the characteristics that describe the workload. The selector
        provides a starting point for deciding whether Dataverse is worth
        evaluating as the business data platform.
      </p>
    </div>

    <span class="dvfs__badge" data-badge aria-live="polite">
      Start with the workload
    </span>
  </div>

  <fieldset class="dvfs__choices">
    <legend class="dvfs__legend">
      Select the characteristics that apply
    </legend>

    <label class="dvfs__choice">
      <input
        type="checkbox"
        name="dataverse-fit"
        value="structured"
      />

      <span class="dvfs__marker" aria-hidden="true">
        <span>✓</span>
      </span>

      <span class="dvfs__choice-body">
        <strong>Structured business data</strong>

        <span>
          The workload needs defined tables, data types, and reusable business
          records rather than loosely structured information.
        </span>

        <small>DATA MODEL · TABLES + COLUMNS</small>
      </span>
    </label>

    <label class="dvfs__choice">
      <input
        type="checkbox"
        name="dataverse-fit"
        value="relationships"
      />

      <span class="dvfs__marker" aria-hidden="true">
        <span>✓</span>
      </span>

      <span class="dvfs__choice-body">
        <strong>Relationships between records</strong>

        <span>
          The solution depends on connected business entities such as people,
          departments, cases, accounts, assets, or transactions.
        </span>

        <small>DATA MODEL · RELATIONSHIPS</small>
      </span>
    </label>

    <label class="dvfs__choice">
      <input
        type="checkbox"
        name="dataverse-fit"
        value="security"
      />

      <span class="dvfs__marker" aria-hidden="true">
        <span>✓</span>
      </span>

      <span class="dvfs__choice-body">
        <strong>Controlled access to data</strong>

        <span>
          The workload needs role-based access, record-level controls,
          environment boundaries, or other governed security patterns.
        </span>

        <small>SECURITY · GOVERNED ACCESS</small>
      </span>
    </label>

    <label class="dvfs__choice">
      <input
        type="checkbox"
        name="dataverse-fit"
        value="platform"
      />

      <span class="dvfs__marker" aria-hidden="true">
        <span>✓</span>
      </span>

      <span class="dvfs__choice-body">
        <strong>Power Platform integration</strong>

        <span>
          The data needs to work closely with Power Apps, Power Automate,
          Dynamics 365, Power Pages, or related Microsoft workloads.
        </span>

        <small>PLATFORM · APPS + AUTOMATION</small>
      </span>
    </label>

    <label class="dvfs__choice">
      <input
        type="checkbox"
        name="dataverse-fit"
        value="governance"
      />

      <span class="dvfs__marker" aria-hidden="true">
        <span>✓</span>
      </span>

      <span class="dvfs__choice-body">
        <strong>Governed application data</strong>

        <span>
          The workload needs a managed data foundation with lifecycle,
          auditing, capacity awareness, and organizational governance.
        </span>

        <small>GOVERNANCE · LIFECYCLE + AUDIT</small>
      </span>
    </label>

    <label class="dvfs__choice">
      <input
        type="checkbox"
        name="dataverse-fit"
        value="api"
      />

      <span class="dvfs__marker" aria-hidden="true">
        <span>✓</span>
      </span>

      <span class="dvfs__choice-body">
        <strong>APIs or pro-code access</strong>

        <span>
          The workload may need Web API, SDK, connectors, custom applications,
          or other integration patterns around the business data.
        </span>

        <small>INTEGRATION · API + SDK</small>
      </span>
    </label>
  </fieldset>

  <div
    class="dvfs__result"
    aria-live="polite"
    aria-atomic="true"
  >
    <div class="dvfs__result-head">
      <div>
        <span class="dvfs__result-kicker">Initial assessment</span>

        <h4 data-title>
          Select the characteristics that apply.
        </h4>
      </div>

      <span class="dvfs__result-level" data-level>
        No assessment yet
      </span>
    </div>

    <p class="dvfs__result-description" data-description>
      This selector is a starting point for workload evaluation, not a final
      architecture or licensing decision.
    </p>

    <div class="dvfs__grid">
      <div class="dvfs__card">
        <span class="dvfs__card-label">What the selection suggests</span>

        <strong data-signal>
          Start by describing the workload.
        </strong>
      </div>

      <div class="dvfs__card">
        <span class="dvfs__card-label">Why it may fit</span>

        <strong data-fit>
          Select one or more characteristics to evaluate Dataverse's role.
        </strong>
      </div>

      <div class="dvfs__card">
        <span class="dvfs__card-label">What to review next</span>

        <strong data-next>
          Consider data model, security, capacity, licensing, and integration
          requirements.
        </strong>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="dvfs__principle">
    <span class="dvfs__principle-mark" aria-hidden="true">→</span>

    <p>
      <strong>Workload first, platform second.</strong>
      Dataverse is valuable when the workload needs the business-data,
      application, security, integration, and governance capabilities it
      provides.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<script>
  const roots = document.querySelectorAll("[data-dvfs]");

  roots.forEach((root) => {
    const badge = root.querySelector("[data-badge]");
    const title = root.querySelector("[data-title]");
    const level = root.querySelector("[data-level]");
    const description = root.querySelector("[data-description]");
    const signal = root.querySelector("[data-signal]");
    const fit = root.querySelector("[data-fit]");
    const next = root.querySelector("[data-next]");

    const checks = Array.from(
      root.querySelectorAll('input[name="dataverse-fit"]')
    );

    if (
      !badge ||
      !title ||
      !level ||
      !description ||
      !signal ||
      !fit ||
      !next
    ) {
      return;
    }

    const state = {
      structured: "Structured business data",
      relationships: "Relationships",
      security: "Security",
      platform: "Power Platform integration",
      governance: "Governance",
      api: "APIs / pro-code access"
    };

    function update() {
      const selected = checks
        .filter((check) => check.checked)
        .map((check) => check.value);

      const count = selected.length;

      root.dataset.state =
        count === 0
          ? "empty"
          : count <= 2
            ? "possible"
            : count <= 4
              ? "good"
              : "strong";

      if (count === 0) {
        badge.textContent = "Start with the workload";
        level.textContent = "No assessment yet";
        title.textContent =
          "Select the characteristics that apply.";
        description.textContent =
          "This selector is a starting point for workload evaluation, not a final architecture or licensing decision.";
        signal.textContent =
          "Start by describing the workload.";
        fit.textContent =
          "Select one or more characteristics to evaluate Dataverse's role.";
        next.textContent =
          "Consider data model, security, capacity, licensing, and integration requirements.";
        return;
      }

      const labels = selected.map((item) => state[item]);

      if (count <= 2) {
        badge.textContent = "POSSIBLE FIT";
        level.textContent = "Evaluate the workload carefully";
        title.textContent =
          "Dataverse may fit, but the workload needs more context.";
        description.textContent =
          "The selected characteristics align with some Dataverse capabilities, but they are not enough by themselves to establish a strong platform fit.";
        signal.textContent =
          `${labels.join(" + ")} are present.`;
        fit.textContent =
          "Compare Dataverse with the existing data source and the workload's security, integration, and lifecycle requirements.";
        next.textContent =
          "Review the data model, access requirements, platform dependencies, expected growth, and licensing.";
        return;
      }

      if (count <= 4) {
        badge.textContent = "GOOD FIT";
        level.textContent = "Dataverse is worth evaluating";
        title.textContent =
          "Several workload characteristics align well with Dataverse.";
        description.textContent =
          "The workload appears to benefit from capabilities that Dataverse is designed to provide for governed business applications.";
        signal.textContent =
          `${labels.length} Dataverse-aligned characteristics selected.`;
        fit.textContent =
          "Dataverse is a strong candidate for the business data layer, especially when Power Platform integration is important.";
        next.textContent =
          "Validate security design, data relationships, capacity, licensing, environments, and integration boundaries.";
        return;
      }

      badge.textContent = "STRONG FIT";
      level.textContent = "Dataverse is a strong candidate";
      title.textContent =
        "The workload closely matches the Dataverse application-data model.";
      description.textContent =
        "The selected requirements point toward governed business data that needs application integration, security, relationships, and lifecycle capabilities.";
      signal.textContent =
        `${labels.length} Dataverse-aligned characteristics selected.`;
      fit.textContent =
        "Start an architecture assessment with Dataverse as the leading business-data option.";
      next.textContent =
        "Design the data model and security boundaries, then validate capacity, licensing, environments, ALM, and operational ownership.";
    }

    checks.forEach((check) => {
      check.addEventListener("change", update);
    });

    update();
  });
</script>

<style>
  .dvfs {
    --dvfs-surface: var(--surface-primary, #ffffff);
    --dvfs-surface-soft: var(--surface-secondary, #f8fafc);
    --dvfs-text: var(--text-primary, #0f172a);
    --dvfs-text-secondary: var(--text-secondary, #475569);
    --dvfs-text-tertiary: var(--text-tertiary, #64748b);
    --dvfs-border: var(--border-default, #dbe3ec);
    --dvfs-border-soft: var(--border-subtle, #e7edf4);
    --dvfs-accent: var(--color-accent, #4ea1e0);
    --dvfs-state: var(--dvfs-accent);

    width: 100%;
    margin-block: var(--space-10, 2.5rem);
    padding: clamp(1.25rem, 3vw, 2rem);
    color: var(--dvfs-text);
    background: var(--dvfs-surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--dvfs-border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg, 0.875rem);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-sm, 0 1px 2px rgb(15 23 42 / 0.06));
  }

  .dvfs[data-state="possible"] {
    --dvfs-state: var(--color-warning, #c2410c);
  }

  .dvfs[data-state="good"] {
    --dvfs-state: var(--color-info, #0f8a8a);
  }

  .dvfs[data-state="strong"] {
    --dvfs-state: var(--color-success, #15803d);
  }

  .dvfs__header {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: var(--space-6, 1.5rem);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-6, 1.5rem);
  }

  .dvfs__eyebrow {
    margin: 0 0 0.25rem;
    color: var(--dvfs-state);
    font-size: var(--font-size-xs, 0.75rem);
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .dvfs h3,
  .dvfs h4,
  .dvfs p {
    margin-top: 0;
  }

  .dvfs h3 {
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
    font-size: clamp(1.3rem, 2vw, 1.6rem);
    line-height: 1.2;
  }

  .dvfs__intro {
    max-width: 70ch;
    margin-bottom: 0;
    color: var(--dvfs-text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .dvfs__badge {
    flex: 0 0 auto;
    align-self: flex-start;
    padding: 0.45rem 0.75rem;
    color: var(--dvfs-state);
    background: color-mix(
      in srgb,
      var(--dvfs-state) 8%,
      var(--dvfs-surface)
    );
    border: 1px solid color-mix(
      in srgb,
      var(--dvfs-state) 30%,
      var(--dvfs-border)
    );
    border-radius: 999px;
    font-size: var(--font-size-xs, 0.75rem);
    font-weight: 600;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .dvfs__choices {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: var(--space-3, 0.75rem);
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    border: 0;
  }

  .dvfs__legend {
    width: 100%;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
    color: var(--dvfs-text);
    font-size: var(--font-size-sm, 0.875rem);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .dvfs__choice {
    position: relative;
    display: block;
    height: 100%;
    padding: 0.95rem;
    background: var(--dvfs-surface-soft);
    border: 1px solid var(--dvfs-border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md, 0.65rem);
    cursor: pointer;
    transition:
      border-color 160ms ease,
      background-color 160ms ease,
      box-shadow 160ms ease,
      transform 160ms ease;
  }

  .dvfs__choice:hover {
    transform: translateY(-1px);
    border-color: var(--dvfs-accent);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-sm, 0 1px 2px rgb(15 23 42 / 0.06));
  }

  .dvfs__choice:has(input:focus-visible) {
    outline: 2px solid var(--dvfs-accent);
    outline-offset: 2px;
  }

  .dvfs__choice input {
    position: absolute;
    width: 1px;
    height: 1px;
    opacity: 0;
    pointer-events: none;
  }

  .dvfs__choice:has(input:checked) {
    border-color: var(--dvfs-state);
    background: color-mix(
      in srgb,
      var(--dvfs-state) 8%,
      var(--dvfs-surface)
    );
    box-shadow:
      inset 0 0 0 1px var(--dvfs-state),
      var(--shadow-sm, 0 1px 2px rgb(15 23 42 / 0.06));
  }

  .dvfs__marker {
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
    width: 1.15rem;
    height: 1.15rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.7rem;
    border: 2px solid var(--dvfs-text-tertiary);
    border-radius: 0.3rem;
    color: transparent;
  }

  .dvfs__marker span {
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    line-height: 1;
  }

  .dvfs__choice:has(input:checked) .dvfs__marker {
    border-color: var(--dvfs-state);
    background: var(--dvfs-state);
    color: var(--dvfs-surface);
  }

  .dvfs__choice-body {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.35rem;
  }

  .dvfs__choice-body strong {
    color: var(--dvfs-text);
    line-height: 1.3;
  }

  .dvfs__choice-body > span {
    color: var(--dvfs-text-secondary);
    font-size: var(--font-size-sm, 0.875rem);
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  .dvfs__choice-body small {
    color: var(--dvfs-text-tertiary);
    font-size: var(--font-size-xs, 0.75rem);
    font-weight: 600;
    line-height: 1.4;
  }

  .dvfs__result {
    margin-top: var(--space-6, 1.5rem);
    padding: 1.2rem;
    background: var(--dvfs-surface-soft);
    border: 1px solid var(--dvfs-border);
    border-left: 4px solid var(--dvfs-state);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md, 0.65rem);
  }

  .dvfs__result-head {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  .dvfs__result-kicker {
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: 0.25rem;
    color: var(--dvfs-text-tertiary);
    font-size: var(--font-size-xs, 0.75rem);
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .dvfs__result h4 {
    margin-bottom: 0;
    color: var(--dvfs-text);
    font-size: var(--font-size-lg, 1.1rem);
    line-height: 1.3;
  }

  .dvfs__result-level {
    flex: 0 0 auto;
    color: var(--dvfs-state);
    font-size: var(--font-size-sm, 0.875rem);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .dvfs__result-description {
    max-width: 72ch;
    margin: 0.65rem 0 0;
    color: var(--dvfs-text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .dvfs__grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: var(--space-3, 0.75rem);
    margin-top: 1rem;
  }

  .dvfs__card {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.35rem;
    padding: 0.9rem;
    background: var(--dvfs-surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--dvfs-border-soft);
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm, 0.5rem);
  }

  .dvfs__card-label {
    color: var(--dvfs-text-tertiary);
    font-size: var(--font-size-xs, 0.75rem);
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .dvfs__card strong {
    color: var(--dvfs-text-secondary);
    font-size: var(--font-size-sm, 0.875rem);
    line-height: 1.55;
  }

  .dvfs__principle {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    margin-top: 1rem;
    padding: 0.9rem 1rem;
    background: var(--dvfs-surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--dvfs-border-soft);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md, 0.65rem);
  }

  .dvfs__principle-mark {
    flex: 0 0 auto;
    color: var(--dvfs-accent);
    font-weight: 800;
  }

  .dvfs__principle p {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--dvfs-text-secondary);
    font-size: var(--font-size-sm, 0.875rem);
    line-height: 1.55;
  }

  @media (max-width: 800px) {
    .dvfs__choices {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .dvfs__grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .dvfs {
      padding: 1rem;
    }

    .dvfs__header {
      display: grid;
      gap: 0.9rem;
    }

    .dvfs__badge {
      justify-self: start;
    }

    .dvfs__result-head {
      align-items: flex-start;
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 0.35rem;
    }
  }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .dvfs__choice {
      transition: none;
    }
  }
</style>
